📑 Project Report: Multi-OS AWS Infrastructure Automation with Ansible🎯

Project Overview
The objective of this project was to automate the lifecycle of a hybrid cloud infrastructure environment using Ansible Core running within Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL). The infrastructure encompasses multi-distribution AWS EC2 instances provisioned via secure, vault-encrypted credentials, automated key-pair integrations, and OS-specific runtime conditionals.🛠️ Task 1: Provisioning Hybrid EC2 Infrastructure via Ansible Loops📋 ObjectiveDeploy three distinct EC2 instances to AWS using an Ansible looping mechanism, delegating the execution locally to the control node.Instance 1 & 2: Ubuntu LTS ServerInstance 3: Amazon Linux / CentOS VariantTarget Region: us-east-1 (N. Virginia)💥 Roadblocks & TroubleshootingEncountered IssueRoot CauseEngineering Resolutionansible-vault: error: unrecognized arguments: -ault-password-fileSyntax Typo: Passed a single dash (-) instead of a double dash (--).Corrected command syntax flags to use full GNU-style double dashes: --vault-password-file.[Errno 8] Exec format error ... vault.passWSL Filesystem Mount Driver Limitation: Creating the plain-text password file inside the Windows mount directory (/mnt/c/...) automatically flagged the file with executable permissions (-rwxrwxrwx). Ansible mistook it for an executable vault script rather than a standard flat text file. Running chmod -x inside /mnt/c/ is silently ignored by the filesystem driver.Relocated vault.pass to the native, isolated Linux home directory structure (~/vault.pass) where native POSIX permissions persist flawlessly. Executed chmod 600 ~/vault.pass to limit access permissions to read-only by the owner.InvalidAMIID.NotFoundCoded standard placeholder AMI strings or region-mismatched image tokens. AMI hashes are isolated globally per cloud region.Identified the explicit active image IDs for us-east-1. Updated the loop sequence parameters to map ami-0e2c8caa4b6378d8c for the Ubuntu instances.InvalidKeyPair.NotFoundPassed an identity string (key_name: "ansible") that did not correspond to a pre-registered cryptographic key pair inside the targeted region workspace.Navigated to the AWS EC2 dashboard, switched to the target region workspace, generated an RSA keypair named explicitly ansible, and downloaded the .pem artifact.📄 Final Blueprint (ec2_create.yaml)yaml---
- name: Infrastructure Lifecycle - Provision Target Lab Nodes
  hosts: localhost
  connection: local
  gather_facts: false

  tasks:
    - name: Spin Up Target Cluster Instances
      amazon.aws.ec2_instance:
        name: "{{ item.name }}"
        key_name: "ansible"
        instance_type: t3.micro
        security_group: default
        region: us-east-1
        aws_access_key: "{{ ec2_access_key }}"
        aws_secret_key: "{{ ec2_secret_key }}"
        network_interfaces:
          - assign_public_ip: true
        image_id: "{{ item.image }}" 
