Use code with caution.🚀 Task 3: Targeted Group Termination via Fact-Gathering Conditionals📋 ObjectiveExecute a selective playbook routine that triggers a system halt command (shutdown) exclusively on nodes belonging to the Debian (Ubuntu) ecosystem while ignoring CentOS/RedHat infrastructure elements.💥 Roadblocks & TroubleshootingEncountered IssueRoot CauseEngineering ResolutionUnrecognized property: becameSyntax error: Misspelled the privilege escalation declaration directive block parameter as became.Standardised the syntax back to its proper key format parameter name: become: true.Conditional logic tracking failureAttempted to process a custom object reference check structure (ansible_facts['os.family']) or introduced string casing typos ('Dedian', 'Redhat').Corrected the syntax lookup string dictionary path reference to ansible_facts['os_family']. Adjusted conditional tracking checks to target the appropriate parent registry family line with strict proper noun capitalisation ('Debian' for Ubuntu distributions; 'RedHat' for enterprise Linux distributions).UNREACHABLE! Connection timed outThe underlying AWS cloud nodes were stopped, terminated, or reassigned new public IP endpoints by the AWS network controller pool.Polled the AWS infrastructure management dashboard, fetched the newly assigned network endpoints, and adjusted the corresponding connection values within inventory.ini.📄 Final Executable Playbook (ec2_stop.yaml)yaml---
- name: Automated Infrastructure Management - Selective Shut Down
  hosts: all
  become: true
  gather_facts: true # Crucial: populates the ansible_facts registry for conditional checks

  tasks: 
    - name: Halt Ubuntu Target Clusters Gracefully
      ansible.builtin.command: /sbin/shutdown -h now
      when: ansible_facts['os_family'] == 'Debian' 
      # Logic: Matches Ubuntu (Debian family), skips Amazon Linux/CentOS (RedHat family)
